From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:40:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 39/40] wasm: preserve paired invocation comparison inputs

Keep inherited uncommitted insert identities fixed in both runtime directions. Treat encoded bytes as opaque scalar values, and verify an exact shared-allocation relation before constructing bounded alternative ID mappings. Equivalent large insert batches can then compare without exhausting a permutation budget, while changed results, reads, and writes remain mismatches.

Validate detached verifier snapshot retention after failed execution as well as success. Extend the warm-entry fixtures to exercise distinct lazy entry preparation, configuration invalidation, preserved dependency hashes, and capability revocation. Preserve the established distinction between derived OCC dependencies and direct-read accounting; no production accounting change is needed.

Validated with the database merge regression, all 35 runnable isolate acceptance tests (three external-artifact fixtures ignored), all 73 feature-enabled function-runner tests, changed-file rustfmt, and scoped library/test clippy. The all-targets clippy invocation remains blocked by pre-existing database benchmark references to removed APIs.
